c3-11647818e833" :question/math-academy-id "q-7595" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=16$ and ${b}^{2}=9.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=16,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be  $a=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=9,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=4,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=3.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 4=8,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 3=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7595/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7595"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7608/selection/9d988a462a7f2a1d6bc7652a55e6289629356acc481d0fd50de39dc26544a0f8" :answer/id #uuid "537c73db-17df-5790-81bb-c7aefd37b84c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7608/selection/7421eb055175e9faf5bcefac56a9209ab3de0697c6a0c50318aa4df2c705cf4d" :answer/id #uuid "f67726da-c546-5c7e-a816-e6f448e62798" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7608/selection/3b9483c9771280da0390d9b48c02cd8f1c7e4f2219475655dc90446b99c894bc" :answer/id #uuid "05b22326-a022-5ce9-8c8f-5b92d6ceb501" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7608/selection/51c8b210bd855fff90ffc7c190027fda5e3019bdf2956d27620cde5b7a993bf9" :answer/id #uuid "8d9cd681-23f6-5056-8efd-fb7f503a8310" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7608/selection/4a861eac0d89336e4ccaa1b516759fefd17ec6f5ca0904e61471627d50915185" :answer/id #uuid "52bf4c3b-47fe-5a95-a6c2-285d65e8b473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7608/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f22fe96-8060-5b94-8510-e4d0d4c2dbd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7608/selection/51c8b210bd855fff90ffc7c190027fda5e3019bdf2956d27620cde5b7a993bf9" :answer-field/choices ["q-7608/selection/9d988a462a7f2a1d6bc7652a55e6289629356acc481d0fd50de39dc26544a0f8" "q-7608/selection/7421eb055175e9faf5bcefac56a9209ab3de0697c6a0c50318aa4df2c705cf4d" "q-7608/selection/3b9483c9771280da0390d9b48c02cd8f1c7e4f2219475655dc90446b99c894bc" "q-7608/selection/51c8b210bd855fff90ffc7c190027fda5e3019bdf2956d27620cde5b7a993bf9" "q-7608/selection/4a861eac0d89336e4ccaa1b516759fefd17ec6f5ca0904e61471627d50915185"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7608" :question/id #uuid "33e8b3ba-6017-5a10-821d-5c72e377f3a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-7608" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975339/assets/202dec2a2e75aa6720181eb925f98999031453f8f1f8822dd86d7a2baab21396.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7608/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7608"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115135/selection/d6f932363650e5fa7a239e1f1b135831bd1e45b7568d09295936343bafdf95bc" :answer/id #uuid "bbe099e2-26ab-52f1-827b-5edf3e83d6fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$50$ and $12.5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115135/selection/1c5499f806a5d2902b17331ecf2cf8833dce6f4a7da9533ed87d1b5b5476b96c" :answer/id #uuid "98d34774-ec2d-59a3-a2cc-a70ee850eb03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$20$ and $10$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115135/selection/527616f5ebac941b1e2a471e9530e77892501814626f6893265e4e7e1597c899" :answer/id #uuid "0f3ab75e-f101-5f93-9447-26bba28956e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ and $2.5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115135/selection/e2a384ffd47965ea538d83060dbf10a43396d0fd5be9222fe5cc8bae5ad70ebe" :answer/id #uuid "c5d8b558-e408-5f5a-8a7d-7543f64857d5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$10$ and $5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115135/selection/7af3e7cb51bcbe2cbd24d1d42cffd6d57473768b545ccea30320c3cd3ed5dafc" :answer/id #uuid "716831a6-3a2c-535b-b464-bfb88d474e55" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$100$ and $25$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115135/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "24cb62ba-b7a1-56fb-bbb4-e161804e0324" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115135/selection/1c5499f806a5d2902b17331ecf2cf8833dce6f4a7da9533ed87d1b5b5476b96c" :answer-field/choices ["q-115135/selection/d6f932363650e5fa7a239e1f1b135831bd1e45b7568d09295936343bafdf95bc" "q-115135/selection/1c5499f806a5d2902b17331ecf2cf8833dce6f4a7da9533ed87d1b5b5476b96c" "q-115135/selection/527616f5ebac941b1e2a471e9530e77892501814626f6893265e4e7e1597c899" "q-115135/selection/e2a384ffd47965ea538d83060dbf10a43396d0fd5be9222fe5cc8bae5ad70ebe" "q-115135/selection/7af3e7cb51bcbe2cbd24d1d42cffd6d57473768b545ccea30320c3cd3ed5dafc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115135" :question/id #uuid "26228f75-ba8b-5cfd-bc2f-68ab172288f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-115135" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{100}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=100$ and ${b}^{2}=25.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=100,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{100}=10.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=10,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=5.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 10=20,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 5=10.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115135/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115135"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279151/field-1/b6430250e6e1dc796e2bae8a1604594f62564c0eb383bc5675130e0ce416db9b" :answer/id #uuid "bdfa7b5b-5f9c-5e7b-a4a8-a96583b2c87d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{12.25}+\\frac{y^2}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279151/field-1/e7cbc621592ec8989403b528c0741e865a8a8538869af6165b791e3398576ec3" :answer/id #uuid "9048d640-b9d2-5409-80ff-6efc19ab7929" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{3.5}+\\frac{y^2}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279151/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "eaa5418f-11d7-5cdc-8dcc-cdfa6cbefc32" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279151/field-1/b6430250e6e1dc796e2bae8a1604594f62564c0eb383bc5675130e0ce416db9b" :answer-field/choices ["q-279151/field-1/b6430250e6e1dc796e2bae8a1604594f62564c0eb383bc5675130e0ce416db9b" "q-279151/field-1/e7cbc621592ec8989403b528c0741e865a8a8538869af6165b791e3398576ec3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279151" :question/id #uuid "ca370114-02f2-595d-bf62-dcbcc65e8ed9" :question/math-academy-id "q-279151" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975339/assets/0f3972825271a2f9471657919ed3669c63e03cd3740a436ab14cc30ed65b73bc.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{7}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{49}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279151/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279151"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-279153"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975339/assets/b12eb6672d263655f9f77eaafbf486a7be5bf9b7673c73fd0d75382d192a658b.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{3}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{9}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{9}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{81}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{81} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
